Implement configurable TUI issue-list columns as saved-view state. Add a columns array to SavedView, keep existing views backward-compatible by defaulting to the current compact list columns, and let built-in views choose a different column set. The TUI list renderer should render rows from the active view column config and drop lower-priority columns as width shrinks. Supported initial columns: id, date, closed, priority, state, title, assignee, points, milestone, tags. Recently Closed should use order=closed.desc and columns that show the closed relative date instead of created date. Closed timestamps are derived from git-meta history, preferring the most recent closed-by/status closed log entry and falling back to created_at when unavailable.